Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: reject NULL vqmmc supplies

The Rockchip SD shutdown path calls mmc_regulator_set_vqmmc() even for
SPI hosts. mmc_spi does not acquire the MMC regulator supplies, leaving
vqmmc NULL. IS_ERR() does not reject NULL, so shutdown dereferences it in
regulator_is_supported_voltage().

Treat NULL like an unavailable regulator, preserving the existing error
return and behavior for valid supplies.

Link: https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/issues/563

--- a/drivers/mmc/core/regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/regulator.c
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ int mmc_regulator_set_vqmmc(struct mmc_host *mmc, struct mmc_ios *ios)
 	int ret, volt, min_uV, max_uV;
 
 	/* If no vqmmc supply then we can't change the voltage */
-	if (IS_ERR(mmc->supply.vqmmc))
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(mmc->supply.vqmmc))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	switch (ios->signal_voltage) {
